{
  "hypothesis": "Optimize the current solution to improve its performance by utilizing OpenMP directives for parallel processing.",
  "transformations": [
    "Add OpenMP directives to parallelize the matrix traversal and sum calculation.",
    "Use parallel reduction to efficiently compute the maximum sum."
  ],
  "sources_kept": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/solution.cpp",
      "content": "/*\n * Original solution with OpenMP directives\n */\n\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n            scanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n    assert(s<n);\n    assert(n<8000);\n    assert(s>0);\n    assert(n>0);\n\n    int sum = 0;\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for(int i=0;i<s;i++) {\n        for(int j=0;j<s;j++) {\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\n        }\n        #pragma omp critical\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",mxSum);\n}\n"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The solution now uses OpenMP directives to parallelize the matrix traversal and sum calculation, and employs parallel reduction to efficiently compute the maximum sum."
}
